strerror_r as the C library declares it

mlibc, as glibc, declares the GNU strerror_r, which returns the message,
when _GNU_SOURCE is defined, as CPython defines it, and the XSI one,
which returns a number, otherwise. Radix's is the GNU one, as glibc's.

diff --git a/Python/fileutils.c b/Python/fileutils.c
index 324d672..c7cd187 100644
--- a/Python/fileutils.c
+++ b/Python/fileutils.c
@@ -3191,6 +3191,8 @@ _Py_strerror(int code)
 #    define Py_STRERROR_R_GNU
 #  elif defined(__ANDROID__) && defined(_GNU_SOURCE)
 #    define Py_STRERROR_R_GNU
+#  elif defined(__radix__) && defined(_GNU_SOURCE)
+#    define Py_STRERROR_R_GNU
 #  endif
 #endif
 
